## Every commit (required for agents)

Use **English** body with detailed change list:

```text
<type>(scope): subject

## Summary
Why this change exists.

## Changes
- Bullet list of all meaningful changes by area (App, Docs, CI, …)
```

See `.github/instructions/commits.instructions.md`.

### No `Co-authored-by` trailers (CI will fail)

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` lines to commit messages — not for Cursor, Copilot, or any tool.
- CI blocks these words anywhere in the message (case-insensitive): `claude`, `anthropic`, `co-authored`.
- Cursor may auto-append `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` — **strip it before committing** or rewrite the commit without that trailer.
- If a bad commit was already pushed: rewrite history (e.g. replay commits with `git commit-tree` and remove the trailer), then `git push --force-with-lease`.

## Build commands (prefer Taskfile)

```bash
task setup && task build && task test
task version:show
open MagSafeGuard.xcodeproj
```

## Security actions (only these five)

`lockScreen`, `soundAlarm`, `forceLogout`, `shutdown`, `customScript`

## Safety

- Do not run/build the armed app without user intent
- No secrets in commits
